<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Como</h1><p class="st-meta">1109 CE – 1335 CE (approx.) · capital Como</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A lakeside city-republic that Milan destroyed in 1127 and Frederick Barbarossa rebuilt, home of the master builders known as the Comacine masters.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Como, at the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-como">Lake Como</a> on the route to the Alpine passes, had consuls by 1109. Its quarrel with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> over the bishopric and lake trade led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war-1118-1127">Ten Years' War</a> of 1118–1127, which ended with Como's destruction.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Como was ruled by consuls and later a podestà. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, it was rebuilt with imperial support in 1159 and remained largely Ghibelline. Its builders and stonemasons, the magistri comacini, worked across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and the city controlled lake shipping and Alpine traffic. In the 13th and 14th centuries the Ghibelline Rusca and Guelph Vittani families fought for control.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1335 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franchino-rusca">Franchino Rusca</a> surrendered the city to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti">Azzone Visconti</a>, and Como became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>, later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Duchy of Milan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1109 CE – 1335 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.77%;width:4.50%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1109 CE – 1335 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Como</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Franchino Rusca</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Como</dd></dl></aside></div>

